// Tests that a launch helper is specialized on scalar arguments its callers
// pass as constants, and that the constants then reach the kernel.
//
// The shape is the common one: a thin fixed-shape wrapper forwards literals
// into a general helper that owns the launch, so the kernel is indexed with
// runtime extents that are in fact 1.  Neither the helper nor the kernel can
// see that on its own -- only the frame above the launch can.
//
// The general caller must keep using the unspecialized kernel.

// RUN: cir-opt --cir-offload-specialize-launch-wrappers \
// RUN:         --cir-offload-specialize-scalar-args %s | FileCheck %s

// The helper is cloned with ne01/ne02/ne03 pinned...
// CHECK-DAG: cir.func {{.*}}@_ZL7generalPKfPflllll$cargs_3v1_4v1_5v1

// ...and the kernel gains a variant with ne01 and the folded ne02*ne03 baked
// in.  Both the original and the specialized kernel survive.
// CHECK-DAG: cir.offload.func @_Z1kPKfPfllll(
// CHECK-DAG: cir.offload.func @_Z1kPKfPfllll$scalarspec_3v1_4v1(

!s64i = !cir.int<s, 64>
!u32i = !cir.int<u, 32>
!u8i = !cir.int<u, 8>
